 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+# Account settings and passkeys
+
+Sign up, sign in, then open Account settings from the header. Accounts, password hashes,
+sessions, WebAuthn challenges, and credentials are stored in SQLite. Passkey sign-in
+updates the stored last-used timestamp and signature counter after verification.
+
+Requires Node.js 22.13 or newer with `node:sqlite`. Set `ACCOUNT_DB_PATH` to a writable
+SQLite file on a persistent volume (default: `.data/accounts.sqlite`). Instances must
+share the same database; use a database service before deploying across hosts.
+Set `WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN` to the canonical HTTPS origin in production; its hostname is the
+RP ID. Localhost can use HTTP. Existing external-service accounts must register locally;
+this application has no access to the external service's account database.
+
+Provider labels and icons use a local subset of the community AAGUID registry;
+unknown or zero AAGUIDs use a generic key icon. Unsupported Signal APIs are skipped.
+If synchronization fails, server changes remain saved and the page shows a warning.
+
